			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Complete Vine notification handler delegation\n\nFinalize the systematic modularization of Mountain's gRPC notification handling by converting all remaining local handler implementations into thin delegation shims that forward to the dedicated `Vine` crate. This includes the complex provider registration logic, SCM management, terminal lifecycle, and various UI notifications.\n\nThe changes simplify Mountain's `Source/Vine/Server/Notification/` modules to single-line wrappers, remove duplicated provider registration code (46+ provider types) from `MountainVinegRPCService.rs`, and relocate that logic into the `VineHost` trait implementation in `VineHostImpl.rs`. The `RegisterLanguageProvider` and `RegisterScmProvider` notifications now delegate entirely to their Vine counterparts, which handle the full DTO construction, logging, and registration workflows.\n\nThis completes the extraction of Cocoon→Mountain notification processing into the library layer, significantly reducing Mountain's code surface and enforcing consistent IPC standards across the project.",
			"SHA": "75a867c0d6f2670c9bd12f652feb4ab36f4693b4"
		}
